# C069: ChangesetIterator keeps a dangling borrowed TableChange pointer
#
# CONFIRMED — static analysis (use-after-free / lifetime)
#
# last_table_change is not an owned reference (session.c:230-238).  Dropping the
# returned object before the next iteration leaves a pointer the iterator writes
# through.  Conversely, destroying the iterator finalizes SQLite state without
# invalidating a surviving TableChange, whose properties then use freed iterator
# and table-name storage.
